  "sale_events": [],
  "body": "Here's your chance to secure a foothold on one of Mission Bay's most sought-after streets, just moments from the beach.\r\n\r\nSet within a well-established cross-lease of six, this three-bedroom residence enjoys its own exclusive, north-facing outdoor area, lovingly maintained and nurtured over the years into a beautifully landscaped garden. Spanning 110sqm (more or less), the home is arranged across two levels in a layout that offers real flexibility for how you choose to live.\r\n\r\nDownstairs, a generously proportioned double bedroom comes complete with its own bathroom — perfectly suited to visiting guests, extended family, or a private space to work from home — alongside a well fitted-out laundry and double internal-access garaging. An additional off-street car park rounds out the practicality, with secure parking increasingly rare this close to the village. Upstairs, two further bedrooms are served by a second bathroom and separate powder room.\r\n\r\nVery liveable as is, the home also offers genuine potential to add value — particularly upstairs, where an updated kitchen would unlock the full potential of this address. Built in the 1970s, it sits within established, leafy grounds well beyond what a typical townhouse or apartment site provides.\r\n\r\nThis is a genuine chance to buy into Mission Bay, close to the café strip, beachfront and waterfront promenade — perfect for the buyer who sees the potential and wants to make it their own.\r\n\r\nTo be sold by auction on Wednesday 4 November 2026, at 10am (unless sold prior).",
